problems.description:
The input describes a singly linked list. Reverse the list and print the
resulting values. The list is represented directly as a sequence of values;
your program must build the nodes before reversing them.

Read a stream of integers. After each new value, print the median of all values
seen so far. For an even count, print the exact median using .5 when necessary;
for example, 2 and 3 produce 2.5.
